# Seven ways to explore data

All data here is fictional. Every figure also has a text/data alternative.

@slider factor = 1 (min: 1, max: 3, label: "Value multiplier")
@slider selected_period = 1 (min: 1, max: 4, label: "Period")
@choice selected_format = "Text" (options: ["Text", "Audio", "Video"], label: "Format")

@data week
period:number | actual:number | target:number
1 | 12 | 15
2 | 18 | 15
3 | 26 | 15
4 | 22 | 15
@end

@data formats
format:text | readers:number
Text | 48
Audio | 32
Video | 20
@end

@data sessions
minutes:number | pages:number
12 | 4
18 | 8
18 | 7
25 | 11
40 | 18
52 | 24
@end

## Lines
@chart line week (x: "period", y: ["actual", "target"], select: selected_period)

## Areas
@chart area week (x: "period", y: row.actual * factor, select: selected_period)

## Grouped bars
@chart bar week (x: "period", y: ["actual", "target"], select: selected_period)

The selected period is **{{ selected_period }}**.

## Scatter
@chart scatter sessions (x: "minutes", y: "pages", title: "Session length and pages")

## Sectors
@chart pie formats (x: "format", y: "readers", select: selected_format)

## An annular view
@chart donut formats (x: "format", y: "readers", select: selected_format)

The selected format is **{{ selected_format }}**.

## Histogram
@chart histogram sessions (x: "minutes", bins: 4, title: "Distribution of session lengths")

The histogram counts observations in intervals; it does not select individual rows.
